From fc8ae667c48f9fc09c0753a2a86ad5d0779c63ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hasan Mehdi <hasanthemehdi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 10:15:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06/15] x1000: UART RX ring buffer, IRQ-safe UIER, TX timeout

The RX side only read while a reader was blocked in uart_rx, and every
RX interrupt while TX was idle saw TDRQ set and released tx_done_sem, so
the next uart_tx could return before its bytes were out and two HCI
packets interleaved on the wire. UIER was read-modify-written from both
thread and IRQ context without masking interrupts.

Now the IRQ always drains the FIFO into a 4 KiB ring (masking RX and
letting RTS hold the remote if it fills), TX is only serviced while a
transfer is in flight, UIER changes are done with IRQs off, writers are
serialised, and uart_tx gives up after 1 s of CTS held off. Adds
uart_rx_tmo and an overrun counter.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
